      "MORTICIA: It's been too long.\nWEDNESDAY: Do it.",
      "MORTICIA: I suppose we're just like any family in the world.\nWEDNESDAY: Here, Catch.",
      "DEBBIE: I can show you all my references. So you'll know I'm not a homicidal maniac.\nMORTICIA: Of course you're not.",
      "MORTICIA: You've had your shots? Measles, mumps, rabies?\nDEBBIE: I just love babies. They're just so sweet and pink and innocent, I just want to grab 'em and squeeze until there's not a breath left in thei…\nDEBBIE: Hello, Pubert. I love you.",
      "MORTICIA: Children?\nMORTICIA: This is Miss Jellinsky, our new nanny. What do we say?\nWEDNESDAY: Be afraid. Be very afraid.\nDEBBIE: Look at you. All cooped up in the house with a new baby. That's not easy, is it?"
    ]
